Fixed-position build fix for Meshtastic Builder.

Upstream commit 94bb21ecc ("2.8: NodeDB shrink, decoupling, and restructuring",
PR #10413) removed the local

  meshtastic_NodeInfoLite *info = getOrCreateMeshNode(getNodeNum());

from NodeDB::NodeDB() but left the #ifdef USERPREFS_FIXED_GPS block still using
it, so any build that defines USERPREFS_FIXED_GPS fails to compile with

  src/mesh/NodeDB.cpp: error: 'info' was not declared in this scope

Upstream CI never sees it: their shipped userPrefs.jsonc keeps all four
USERPREFS_FIXED_GPS* keys commented out, so the block is never compiled there.
This builder sets USERPREFS_FIXED_GPS whenever the user asks for a fixed
position, so every 2.8.x build with a fixed position hits it.

The hunk below is upstream's own fix, taken verbatim from

  https://github.com/meshtastic/firmware/pull/11825

which was merged into the firmware `develop` branch on 2026-09-12 as df47f95ff.
No released tag contains it yet: v2.8.0.47db0e3, the newest tag, is dated
2026-08-31. data/build_options.json gates this patch on
fixedGpsPatch.fixedSinceFirmwareVersion; set that to the first tag that ships
the fix and the patch stops being applied.

Applies to v2.8.0.7239fe8 and v2.8.0.47db0e3. Tags below 2.8.0 still declare
`info` and compile the block as-is, so they are excluded by
fixedGpsPatch.minFirmwareVersion.

diff --git a/src/mesh/NodeDB.cpp b/src/mesh/NodeDB.cpp
index b0b3df57b7b..d48d9746250 100644
--- a/src/mesh/NodeDB.cpp
+++ b/src/mesh/NodeDB.cpp
@@ -708,11 +708,18 @@ NodeDB::NodeDB()
 #if !MESHTASTIC_EXCLUDE_POSITIONDB
         {
             concurrency::LockGuard guard(&satelliteMutex);
-            nodePositions[info->num] = TypeConversions::ConvertToPositionLite(fixedGPS);
+            nodePositions[getNodeNum()] = TypeConversions::ConvertToPositionLite(fixedGPS);
         }
+        // nodePositions is a member map, so the nodeDatabase CRC compare above cannot see this write -
+        // and it has already run. Flag the segment or the fixed position is only persisted by chance.
+        saveWhat |= SEGMENT_NODEDATABASE;
 #endif
-        nodeDB->setLocalPosition(fixedGPS);
+        setLocalPosition(fixedGPS);
         config.position.fixed_position = true;
+        // Same for config, whose CRC compare also ran before this block. Keep that compare's
+        // degraded-boot guard so an unreadable config is never overwritten with UNSET defaults.
+        if (!configDecodeFailed)
+            saveWhat |= SEGMENT_CONFIG;
 #endif
     }
 #endif
